Task 1: Create a Static Inventory File in YAML Format
Subtask 1.1: Understanding Static Inventory Structure

Static inventories are files that define the hosts and groups that Ansible will manage. Unlike dynamic inventories that query external systems, static inventories are manually maintained files that provide complete control over host organization.

Key Benefits of Static Inventories:

    Predictable: Host definitions remain consistent
    Version Controlled: Can be stored in Git repositories
    Flexible: Support complex grouping and variable structures
    Secure: No external API calls required

