Subtask 2.5: Advanced Inventory Operations

Demonstrate advanced inventory management techniques:

# Create a script to validate inventory
nano scripts/validate-inventory.sh

#!/bin/bash

INVENTORY_FILE="inventories/production/hosts.yml"

echo "=== Inventory Validation Report ==="
echo "Date: $(date)"
echo "Inventory File: $INVENTORY_FILE"
echo

echo "=== All Hosts ==="
ansible-inventory -i $INVENTORY_FILE --list --yaml | grep -A 1 "hosts:"

echo
echo "=== Group Structure ==="
ansible-inventory -i $INVENTORY_FILE --graph

echo
echo "=== Host Count by Group ==="
for group in webservers databases loadbalancers monitoring; do
    count=$(ansible-inventory -i $INVENTORY_FILE --list | jq -r ".${group}.hosts | length" 2>/dev/null || echo "0")
    echo "$group: $count hosts"
done

echo
echo "=== Connectivity Test ==="
ansible -i $INVENTORY_FILE all -m ping --one-line

echo
echo "=== Variable Validation ==="
ansible-inventory -i $INVENTORY_FILE --list | jq '.all.vars' 2>/dev/null || echo "No global variables found"

# Make the script executable
chmod +x scripts/validate-inventory.sh

# Run the validation script
./scripts/validate-inventory.sh

Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: YAML Syntax Errors

Problem: Inventory file fails to parse due to YAML syntax errors.

Solution:

# Validate YAML syntax
python3 -c "import yaml; yaml.safe_load(open('inventories/production/hosts.yml'))"

# Use ansible-inventory to check for errors
ansible-inventory -i inventories/production/hosts.yml --list

Issue 2: Host Connectivity Problems

Problem: Ansible cannot connect to hosts defined in inventory.

Solution:

# Test SSH connectivity manually
ssh -i ~/.ssh/id_rsa webadmin@192.168.1.10

# Check SSH configuration
ansible -i inventories/production/hosts.yml web01.example.com -m setup

# Debug connection issues
ansible -i inventories/production/hosts.yml web01.example.com -m ping -vvv

Issue 3: Variable Precedence Issues

Problem: Variables not applying as expected due to precedence conflicts.

Solution:

# Check variable precedence for a specific host
ansible-inventory -i inventories/production/hosts.yml --host web01.example.com

# Debug variable sources
ansible-playbook -i inventories/production/hosts.yml playbooks/inventory-demo.yml --limit web01.example.com -vv

Best Practices for Static Inventory Management
1. Organization Structure

    Use consistent directory structures
    Separate inventories by environment
    Group related hosts logically
    Use meaningful naming conventions

2. Variable Management

    Place common variables in group_vars/all.yml
    Use group-specific variables for shared configurations
    Reserve host_vars for truly unique settings
    Document variable purposes and dependencies

3. Security Considerations

    Store sensitive data in Ansible Vault
    Use SSH keys instead of passwords
    Limit inventory file permissions
    Regular security audits of access patterns

4. Maintenance Practices

    Version control inventory files
    Regular validation and testing
    Document inventory changes
    Implement change approval processes

